 "findings": [
  "Gait switches mostly work (walk->trot 10/10, trot->canter 9/10, canter->trot 7/9, trot->walk 7/7). The falls are sideways (roll ~1 rad when the uprightness drops below 0.5) 0.5-0.8 s after the switch, at 1.7-2 m/s. The 'canter' is not a real canter: Bolt makes ~1.2 m/s of the dog's 3.3 m/s, so the canter clip is mostly a different trot.",
  "walk->sit never falls but only 1 in 10 is a sit: at 1 m/s the sit clip (a dog standing still, then sitting) makes Bolt brake by folding the front legs, and it ends nose DOWN (pitch -0.5 rad, the clip has +0.6) at 20 cm. From that pose the lie clip tips it over (9/10 falls, 1.35 s in, nose down and rolled 0.6 rad). From standing still the same chain works every time (sit 10/10 in pose, lie 10/10, posture stand 10/10). Starting the sit clip at its start instead of the closest pose (8/8 fell), or braking first with the posture brain's stand (6-8 of 8 fell), did not help.",
  "Jumps from a trot: the jump brain learned from a standstill 45-65 cm away; handed over at 1.1 m from a 1.5-1.9 m/s trot it clears 20 cm 8/10 and 30 cm 7/10 cleanly, but 40 cm only 3/10 (every failure knocked the bar: the trailing legs clip it; 1 in 10 also crashes). The bigger problem is after the landing: Bolt lands at 3-4 m/s, faster than any clip the dog-motion brain can hold, and falls sideways within 0.5-2 s in 17 of 26 landings, at every height (a 0.6 s canter bridge did not measurably help).",
  "Recovery works: every shove topples Bolt, self-righting + tuck + stand stands it up 9/10 (the 10th ends at 38 cm, just under the bar), and walking off after it works 9/9.",
  "What would fix them: train the transitions instead of only the skills. (1) Imitation training that switches clips mid-try at the closest pose (exactly what skills.py does) and starts sit/lie from moving walk/trot states, or a 'stop' clip, so it learns to brake before sitting. (2) The jump brain trained from a running approach (tries that start from recorded trot states 1-2 m before the bar) and continuing 2 s into the trot reward after landing, or the dog-motion brain given starts from the jump brain's landings (3-4 m/s). (3) A real canter (run 18c/22) so fast landings have a gait to go to."
 ]
